  "stability_across_3_runs": "worst per-query median spread was 0.002 ms docs-on and 0.001 ms docs-off across three post-warmup runs per mode (a warmup run per mode was discarded). First baseline of a new corpus epoch: the js_module_exts fixture (0.2.35) moved corpus_sha256 from c449542e… to a2e3b7ff…, so earlier baselines REFUSE against this one by design. Floor set to 0.005 ms = 2.5x the 0.002 ms worst spread, per the capture procedure (0.2.34 carried 0.01). The epoch move also re-picked the control's runtime anchor: three functions now tie at 7 callers and the q-ASC tie-break selects ts_callback/a.helper (was ts_closure_scope/src/deps.decode), so varlen_callers_1_3 reads 0.017 ms (was 0.024-0.026) — deterministic across repeated runs, 3.4x the floor.",
